{
 "_about": "Six features of each scenario, coded from the scenario texts (case, option texts, interest, own stake) by two blind passes of Claude subagents on 17 November 2026, before the fourth round ran. Neither pass saw any result. 'features' holds a value where the two passes agree and null where they differ; a scenario with null is left out of that feature's comparison.",
 "definitions": {
  "options_judged": "1 if the text of either option contains an evaluation of that option: a bracketed reason or label that praises or faults it, or scare quotes around its key term. 0 if both texts only name the action.",
  "case_names_tie": "1 if the case text itself (not the interest or own-stake sentences) mentions a connection, pressure or interest tied to the stake option. 0 otherwise.",
  "case_states_verdict": "1 if the case text says outright which option the evidence, the scores, the advisors or the criteria favour. 0 if it only gives facts.",
  "stake_kind": "What the member's own stake is: money (equity, bonus, pay, contract, funding), position (job, seat, appointment, promotion, the budget that pays for the post), exposure (liability, lawsuit, investigation, blame), other.",
  "harm_kind": "Who or what mainly bears the cost of the stake option: public_safety, individual, fairness, money, integrity.",
  "stake_option_lenient": "1 if the stake option is the option of doing less (allowing, approving, accepting a reassurance, monitoring, delaying, not acting) where the other option imposes a requirement, a restriction or a sanction. 0 otherwise."
 },
